From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 16:41:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] webservices: Fault the reader on malformed input, and give
 WS_ERROR the strings Windows gives it.

As measured on Windows 11 build 29671:
- an end tag must close the innermost element, by the same name and case; a character XML does not allow, in
  text or in an attribute value, is malformed input too, text before it being read as a node of its own;
- malformed input faults the reader: WsReadNode, WsReadStartElement, WsReadToStartElement, WsReadEndElement,
  WsSkipNode, WsFillReader, WsReadType and WsGetReaderProperty then fail with WS_E_OBJECT_FAULTED until WsSetInput,
  WsGetReaderNode still giving the node the reader stopped on, and WsReadType checking its arguments first;
- WsReadStartElement on text or an end element, or on text at the top of the document, is malformed input;
- WsReadToStartElement does not pass over text that is not whitespace, moves onto an end element, and tells
  whether the element has the local name and namespace asked for;
- WsReadType of a simple type on an element reads the element's text;
- WsSetInput with an encoding type that is none, and WsCreateServiceProxyFromTemplate with a template type that
  is none, fail with E_INVALIDARG.

The error object of a call gets what Windows puts into it, in the error's language (English and Simplified
Chinese here, word for word): the row and column of malformed input, what was wrong with it, the faulted reader,
a heap too small, a reader property or encoding type that is not one, a type that failed to read, an int32 that
does not parse, and a policy description or template type that is wrong.  The error parameter of the other calls
is taken as well, without a FIXME.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

